## Why This Is Asked
Tests a clean DP formulation for segmentation with per-placement costs and wildcards. It also probes backtracking and memoization versus tabulation choices under a dictionary constraint.

## Key Concepts
- DP on string positions with a dictionary
- Memoization vs bottom-up tabulation
- Backtracking reconstruction of segmentation
- Handling wildcards and per-placement costs

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCost(s, dict) {
  const n = s.length;
  const memo = new Array(n+1).fill(null);
  const choice = new Array(n).fill(null);

  function costAt(i, w) {
    let cost = 0;
    for (let j = 0; j < w.length; j++) {
      if (s[i+j] !== '?' && s[i+j] !== w[j]) {
        cost++;
      }
    }
    return cost;
  }

  function dp(i) {
    if (i === n) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== null) return memo[i];

    let best = Infinity;
    let bestWord = null;

    for (const w of dict) {
      if (i + w.length <= n) {
        const c = costAt(i, w) + dp(i + w.length);
        if (c < best) {
          best = c;
          bestWord = w;
        }
      }
    }

    memo[i] = best;
    choice[i] = bestWord;
    return best;
  }

  const minCost = dp(0);
  if (minCost === Infinity) return -1;

  // Reconstruct segmentation
  const words = [];
  let i = 0;
  while (i < n) {
    words.push(choice[i]);
    i += choice[i].length;
  }

  return { cost: minCost, words };
}
```

## Complexity
Time: O(n × sum|w|) where sum|w| is total length of all dictionary words
Space: O(n) for memoization and choice arrays

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses your ability to design a compact prefix-search data structure and implement tie-breaking logic using a Trie.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with terminal frequencies stored at each node
- Prefix search via traversal to the prefix end node
- DFS collection of all words in the subtree
- Sorting by frequency (descending), then lexicographic order for ties

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.freq = 0;
  }
}

class Autocomplete {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  addWord(word, freq) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }
    node.freq = freq;
  }

  getSuggestions(prefix, limit) {
    if (limit <= 0) return [];

    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) return [];
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }

    const results = [];
    const dfs = (currentNode, path) => {
      if (currentNode.freq > 0) {
        results.push({ word: path, freq: currentNode.freq });
      }
      for (const [char, childNode] of currentNode.children) {
        dfs(childNode, path + char);
      }
    };

    dfs(node, prefix);

    results.sort((a, b) => {
      if (b.freq !== a.freq) return b.freq - a.freq;
      return a.word.localeCompare(b.word);
    });

    return results.slice(0, limit).map(r => r.word);
  }
}
```
